        "title": "Installing Mariadb 10.6 on Windows Server",
        "excerpt":"      Install MariaDB 10.6  on Windows Server   Click Here to download  MariaDB-10.6 from the official MariaDB website.      Execute the installer and click Next.      Accept the License Agreement and click Next.      In the Custom Setup section select MariaDB Server and click Next.      Set the root user password for MariaDB, then click Next.      In Default Instance Properties section leave the default values and click Next.      Feedback plugin can be enabled or disabled in the checkbox then click Next.      Click Install to begin the MariaDB installation.      Click Finish to complete the installation.      MariaDB has been successfully installed on your windows server.   Now dd the System Environmental Variables for MariaDB by following the below steps:   Right click on This PC, go to *Properties &gt; Advanced System Settings &gt; Environment Variables.         Now click on Path &gt; Edit &gt; New &amp; add path C:\\Program Files\\MariaDB 10.6\\bin here and click OK in all 3 tabs.         ","categories": [],
